I slowly return to my quiet home.
I drink water and take my first medicine.
There is a lot of pain in my body.
Suddenly, there is a noise at the door.
I open the door.
My neighbor Asha is standing there.
Her dog Moti is also there.
Asha asks, "Maya, how are you?"
I say, "I am not well today."
"There is still pain in my head."
Asha says, "You should rest."
"Do not worry."
Moti wags his tail and looks at me.
I smile and pet him.
I say thank you to Asha.
She goes to her home.
I close the door and go to my bed.
I lie down on the bed and close my eyes.
I soon fall asleep.
